{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "28c19eb6-6963-8314-a787-9d5bd3590753",
  "created_at": "2026-01-11T15:54:53-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Walter Brownell",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:50:23-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Lorraine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:50:27-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, is it all right if I ask you something about a flooded street? I know it's Sunday, City Hall's closed, so I'm calling the storm line like the recording said."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:50:41-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Absolutely, that's what this line is for on weekends. What's going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:50:47-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So, the street in front of my house is a pond. A real pond. It's the coastal storm from Friday, the one that ended yesterday, and it's still sitting there. Cars keep going through and they're throwing wakes up onto the sidewalk, onto my steps."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:51:07-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that's no good. Can I get the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:51:12-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Two twenty-nine Ayrault Street. Up on the Hill. Is it all right if I say this keeps happening? Every time we get real rain, the water just sits and nobody comes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:51:26-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, two twenty-nine Ayrault Street, standing water in the road, and it's been there since the storm. Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:51:36-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that's right. I'm the landlord on the building, I'm not even in it, I'm just driving past to check on the tenants right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:51:48-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Is the water up to the house, or just in the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:51:55-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just the street so far, but it's deep. Over the curb on the low side. And, um, the older woman next door can't get out. She's got a walker, she's not going to wade through that, and she can't get to her car."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:52:14-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Is she safe in the house? Does she need anything emergency, like medical?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:52:21-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, she's okay, I knocked. She just can't leave. But that's not right, is it? A person stuck inside because the drain won't take the water."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:52:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I understand. I'm going to put it in as a flooded roadway with a neighbor who's blocked in, so it gets looked at with some priority."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:52:45-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Sorry, is it all right if I ask, do the crews work weekends? Because I'd hate for this to sit till Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:52:56-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They do come out on weekends after a storm, yes. The storm line goes to the on-call people, and I'll flag this one for them today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:53:08-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. [pause] Hang on, sorry. What? No, I'm on the phone with the city. [pause] Sorry, my teenager's in the back seat asking why we're parked here and whether the car's going to float. Is it all right if I just ignore that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:53:27-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Go ahead, tell them the city's working on it. Let me read this back. Two twenty-nine Ayrault Street, road flooded since Saturday's storm, vehicles creating wakes, elderly neighbor unable to leave. Anything to add?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:53:42-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it exactly. I'd just say, it's been like this before. I called last winter and got told someone would look at the drain, and then, nothing I could see."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:53:56-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. I don't see the details of that from here, but I'll note that it's a recurring spot so whoever picks it up knows."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:08-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd appreciate that. Honestly I'm tired of it. Is it all right if I leave my number in case they want to reach me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:19-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:21-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 401-555-0199."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:23-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four oh one, five five five, oh one nine nine. And it's Walter?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:29-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Walter Brownell, B-R-O-W-N-E-L-L."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:31-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Mr. Brownell. It's in. Somebody from the on-call crew should be heading over, and if you see them, you can tell them about your neighbor."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:43-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks for picking up on a Sunday. I'll keep an eye out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-11T15:54:49-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Drive carefully through that water."
    }
  ],
